  "note": "The McConnell household on the 1901 return, transcribed by A. Hagues, filed at Gleadthorpe, 11 Cavendish Crescent North (#27) on A. Hagues's reading, not Flixton as this file first had it. Wright's Directory of Nottingham 1894-95 prints 'Gleadthorpe, Jno. M'Connell, warehouse manager' on Cavendish Crescent North, and Flixton was Sir Samuel G. Johnson's then. The head is the record's '? McConnell' (#2836), bound by number so his 1901 census record goes on him and no second John McConnell is made; his forename still needs changing from '?' to John by hand, and the record still lists him as a resident of Flixton (#30), which wants removing. Gleadthorpe already holds a 1901 census record for William Henry Radford (#3200), engineer, as head with no age: the directories print him on the line after Gleadthorpe, a different house, so that record is probably misfiled; it is left as an open question rather than moved. Everyone else here is new to the record. Ages are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way.",
  "source": "1901 census, transcribed by A. Hagues. Directory evidence: Wright's Directory of Nottingham 1894-95, page 44 (Leicester Special Collections id 164550); 1898-99, page 50 (id 165226); 1910-11, page 65 (id 165741).",
